### Page 4 of 12

```text
Expedited Plat/UDC-18-00102
3
EXPEDITED REVIEW:
This plat is being pursued as an expedited application.  An expedited review process is a concurrent
preliminary and final plat. A project may be eligible for an expedited review when the proposal contains
no significant planning, design or engineering issues.  In other words, proposals that meet all applicable
regulations and generally meet the review criteria for preliminary and final plat may be eligible for the
concurrent preliminary and final plat process.

Due to meeting the expedited plat criteria set forth in Section 2.1.2.c(3) of the Cheyenne Unified
Development Code, Staff recommends allowing the plat to proceed as an expedited application.

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:
This plat application proposes extinguishing easements on one lot in the County. The easements being
removed are no longer necessary to service the Woods Landing Estates development. Regional
easements and easements still needed to service the development remain in place.

This land is outside the Urban Service Boundary in an area designated as Rural Residential by
PlanCheyenne. This property is expected to develop as low-density residential without connection to
urban services such as sewer. The current lot meets these expectations. This land is zoned County AR,
and the lot is not changing size or shape. The proposed plat will not create any undue influence upon
infrastructure, the surrounding area, or future development.

Due to meeting the review criteria set forth in Section 2.1.2.d and 2.1.3.d of the Cheyenne
Unified Development Code, staff recommends the Planning Commission approve this
expedited plat, advancing the final plat to the Governing Body.
```

