```text
Expedited Plat/UDC-18-00102
6

PRELIMINARY PLAT DATA:  In reviewing, providing comments, and making recommendations and
decisions on a proposed preliminary plat, the Staff, Planning Commission and City Council shall use the
following 8 criteria, as found in Section 2.1.2.d:

1. PLANCHEYENNE - The application is in accordance
with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in PlanCheyenne.

This application is in conformance with
PlanCheyenne.

The future land use map identifies the subject
property and most of the immediately surrounding
area as Rural Residential and outside the Urban
Service Boundary. This land is expected to develop
with rural residential-style development, and the
existing lots match the expected style of
development.

Land to the south is designated Urban Transition
Residential and is within the Urban Service
Boundary. This land to the South is expected to
develop with lower-density urban residential uses
within City limits and connected to City services.
This plat will not unduly affect the ability of the land
to the south to develop as anticipated.

2. PLANNING - The application reflects sound planning and urban design principles with respect to
existing and potential future development in the vicinity, including consideration of current and future
streets, open spaces, blocks and lots, and public utilities or facilities.

This application proposes extinguishes easements on one lot in a previously platted area. The
application will not have an adverse effect on the current infrastructure.

3. SUBDIVISION STANDARDS - Division of land meets the purposes, intent, and all applicable standards in
Article 4.

Transportation Network:
The transportation network in this area of the County is well established and no additions to the
street network are proposed.

