### Page 8 of 12

```text
Expedited Plat/UDC-18-00102
7
Community Facility Fees:
This land is not within City limits. Plat fees are not required unless this property annexes to the
City in the future. If annexed, Park Acquisition and Infrastructure Fees would be due at
$3,360(4.8 acres at $350/acre for each fee).
Open Space:
This division of land is not required to provide open space.

4. PHASING - Any phasing proposed in the application is clearly indicated and demonstrates a logical and
well-planned development pattern. This may include consideration of amenities and public facilities of the
subdivision within each phase compared to the anticipated timing or the likelihood of future phases being
constructed as planned.

No phasing is proposed with this project.

5. STUDIES - The impacts identified in specific studies or technical reports that were prepared or
requested to be prepared in association with the application, and whether the findings and
recommendations of these reports, or any modifications or conditions on approval of the application, can
mitigate these impacts.

The applicant re-submitted the Drainage and Traffic Studies associated with the original Woods
Landing Estates Plat (in 2016). Traffic and Drainage Worksheets were also submitted for just this plat
area. The applicant also submitted a waiver of Environmental Impact Assessment request, as the
proposed development pattern of the land ently proposed. Engineering and Environmental Health
found no major issues with the project as presented.

6. ZONING - All proposed lots shall be buildable lots
according to the existing or proposed zoning district
standards, and result in site design and development
patterns that meet the Intent and Applicability
statements of the existing or proposed zoning district.
All parcels not proposed as buildable lots and which
are not dedicated to and accepted by the City shall
have a clearly defined entity responsible for ongoing
maintenance.

This land is currently zoned County AR. The
proposed lot is similar in size to surrounding
parcels, and no changes to the current lot size is
proposed.

Map #4 – Zone Districts
Source: Cheyenne/Laramie County GIS
Cooperative Program
